<configuration>

    <appender name="CONSOLE" class="ch.qos.logback.core.ConsoleAppender">
        <encoder>
            <pattern>%d{HH:mm:ss.SSS} [%thread] %-5level %logger{36} - %msg%n</pattern>
        </encoder>
    </appender>

    <!--
        There is deliberately no unreferenced appender here. A FileAppender writing readmodel.log
        survived the deletion of BenchmarkApplication, and an appender nothing refers to makes logback
        log a WARN about it, which in turn makes logback dump its whole configuration status to
        stderr: roughly twenty-five lines. A JMH profile starts one JVM per fork per workload per
        target, so a nine-workload two-target run paid that toll seventy-two times and buried the
        measurements in about two thousand lines of configuration chatter.

        Note for whoever edits these comments: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment, and
        logback fails the whole configuration on a parse error rather than falling back, so every
        fork then dies in LoggerFactory before it reaches a benchmark. Write "which" or a colon.
    -->

    <!--
        The banner is twelve lines of ASCII art per JVM, which is charming once and unreadable
        seventy-two times. Silenced here only, in the benchmark harness; nothing else sets this.
    -->
    <logger name="org.sliceworkz.Banner" level="WARN"/>

    <root level="INFO">
        <appender-ref ref="CONSOLE"/>
    </root>

</configuration>